A||N||6||darkmagic||help with parking lights||||1||
Z||000000||darkmagic||07-21-2001||12:26 AM||||I have a problem with my parking lights not functioning properly.<P>With the switch turned on, the rear parking lights work (rear lamps and read side lamps) but the front side lamps and front turn lamps do not work.<P>The turn signals work, but another weird thing is that when the parking lights are on, the dash shows the parking lights constantly on. both signals are on in the dash but not operating in the front.<P>help! i have no idea what is wrong.. my guess is a ground is bad.. but can someone tell me how to fix this! <P>TIA||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||07-21-2001||12:39 AM||||Your saying that when you turn on your parking lights.... The turn signal indicators (green arrows stay on)?<P>If that is the case. Clean the front turn signal sockets & replace the bulbs. Inspect the sockets closely. They tend to corrode over time. You might have to replace them...<P>Good luck..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><I>Haze</I><P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">  <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||10
Z||000002||darkmagic||07-21-2001||12:41 AM||||yeah.. the lights are always on on the dash... <P>corroded limp sockets eh.. hmm<P>can i replace them myself? (i'm handy.. but i'm no mechanic)<P>how much should those sockets cost? anyone have any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Haze_Performance||07-21-2001||12:54 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by darkmagic:<BR><B>yeah.. the lights are always on on the dash... <P>corroded limp sockets eh.. hmm<P>can i replace them myself? (i'm handy.. but i'm no mechanic)<P>how much should those sockets cost? anyone have any ideas?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yes, you can replace them yourself. You just cut the old ones off (3 wires each)& splice the new ones on and wrap with electrical tape. Its VERY easy. The sockets are under $12.00 each new from a local parts store. But check them first. You might just need to clean them & put new bulbs in.<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">  <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000004||darkmagic||07-21-2001||12:58 AM||||I actually did replace the bulbs but there was some major green stuff flying out when i changed the bulbs. I should take them out again and clean them out more thoroughly.<P>I clean them again and try it and see if that helps... if not.. i'll splurge and get new sockets..<P>do you think that will cure the parking lights for the front and getting them to work with the back?<P>I don't get why the rear would work and the front wouldn't.<P>thanks for your help haze.. i appreciate it. I'll let you know what happens...||||reg||1
Z||000005||Haze_Performance||07-21-2001||01:14 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by darkmagic:<BR><B>I actually did replace the bulbs but there was some major green stuff flying out when i changed the bulbs. I should take them out again and clean them out more thoroughly.<P>I clean them again and try it and see if that helps... if not.. i'll splurge and get new sockets..<P>do you think that will cure the parking lights for the front and getting them to work with the back?<P>I don't get why the rear would work and the front wouldn't.<P>thanks for your help haze.. i appreciate it. I'll let you know what happens...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Heres my experience with the front lights:<P>I was driving and I used the left turn signal. After the turn the left dash light did not go off. When I got home I walked around the car and checked all the lights. All worked except the left front & side markerlight. I knew that it was just a light so I let it slide until the next day. I went out in the morning (Forgot about the burnt out light) & went about my day. By the time I got home that night the right front went out. I pulled the lens off of the bumper & saw that one of the sockets were bad & both lights were dead. I cut off both the old sockets & replaced them. Now everything is good. No further problems.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.ws6fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indyclick.gif">   <BR></A><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="red"><B>Click above to visit my website.</B></FONT></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 07-21-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000006||darkmagic||07-22-2001||09:41 PM||||Haze,<P>both sockets have been changed and the problems are gone! exactly like you mentioned.<P>Thanks for all of your help!||||reg||1
